/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The United Nations Voluntary Trust Fund for Victims of Trafficking in Persons, Especially Women and Children \(UNVTF\) was established in July 2010 by the UN General Assembly, through the adoption of Resolution 64/293, endorsing the United Nations Global Plan of Action to Combat Trafficking in Persons. )
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Administered by the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime \(UNODC\) on behalf of the UN System, the Trust Fund's mandate is to provide humanitarian, legal and financial aid to victims of trafficking in persons through the awarding of multi-year grants to specialized civil society organizations \(CSOs\) who are on the frontlines of tackling human trafficking and providing key victims assistance.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
