/S /H3
/T (The report has been prepared by the UN Office on Drugs and Crime \(UNODC\), which manages the UNVTF Secretariat out of Vienna, Austria. In its capacity, UNODC has overseen the allocation of resources, monitoring of funded project and the coordination of efforts aimed at providing relief and support to victims of human trafficking.)
/E (The report has been prepared by the UN Office on Drugs and Crime \(UNODC\), which manages the UNVTF Secretariat out of Vienna, Austria. In its capacity, UNODC has overseen the allocation of resources, monitoring of funded project and the coordination of efforts aimed at providing relief and support to victims of human trafficking.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The report covers the period from 1 January to 31 December 2023 and presents a deep-dive account of select narrative, results-based outcomes, and financial data associated with the Trust Fund's activities during this time. It outlines the specific progress made by the Trust Fund, including the projects funded, and highlights the positive impact these efforts have had on the ground. The information contained in this report is drawn from various sources, including project reports submitted by NGO grantees, financial statements, as well as on-site and virtual monitoring visits conducted to ensure the effective implementation and oversight of the projects.)
/E (The report covers the period from 1 January to 31 December 2023 and presents a deep-dive account of select narrative, results-based outcomes, and financial data associated with the Trust Fund's activities during this time. It outlines the specific progress made by the Trust Fund, including the projects funded, and highlights the positive impact these efforts have had on the ground. The information contained in this report is drawn from various sources, including project reports submitted by NGO grantees, financial statements, as well as on-site and virtual monitoring visits conducted to ensure the effective implementation and oversight of the projects.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
