/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/T (Hagar International  provided safe accommodation, medical support, education, and reintegration services to 76 Afghan girls who were trafficked or at high risk of exploitation. Of these, 41 girls have successfully reintegrated, while the remaining continue to receive support in the shelter. The shelter served girls facing human trafficking, domestic violence, homelessness, and health issues.  An in-house nurse attended to urgent health needs, with medicine supplied directly in the shelter. )
/E (Hagar International  provided safe accommodation, medical support, education, and reintegration services to 76 Afghan girls who were trafficked or at high risk of exploitation. Of these, 41 girls have successfully reintegrated, while the remaining continue to receive support in the shelter. The shelter served girls facing human trafficking, domestic violence, homelessness, and health issues.  An in-house nurse attended to urgent health needs, with medicine supplied directly in the shelter. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 24 0 R
