515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Tadamun Social Society \(TASS\) played a pivotal role in the repatriation of 50 young trafficking victims, including 12 Ethiopians and 38 Somalis, aged 13 to 17. Through close collaboration with community structures, child protection committees, police checkpoints, and courts, TASS identified the victims. One critical aspect of TASS's support was family tracing, where efforts were made to reconnect these girls with their families in Somalia and Ethiopia. This process was vital in restoring a sense of belonging and security, which is key to their emotional recovery. TASS's repatriation efforts went beyond reuniting families; the organization provided reintegration support, including psychosocial counseling, life skills training, and access to education, ensuring the girls could reintegrate into society and avoid the risk of re-trafficking.)
/E (Tadamun Social Society \(TASS\) played a pivotal role in the repatriation of 50 young trafficking victims, including 12 Ethiopians and 38 Somalis, aged 13 to 17. Through close collaboration with community structures, child protection committees, police checkpoints, and courts, TASS identified the victims. One critical aspect of TASS's support was family tracing, where efforts were made to reconnect these girls with their families in Somalia and Ethiopia. This process was vital in restoring a sense of belonging and security, which is key to their emotional recovery. TASS's repatriation efforts went beyond reuniting families; the organization provided reintegration support, including psychosocial counseling, life skills training, and access to education, ensuring the girls could reintegrate into society and avoid the risk of re-trafficking.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
>>
