527 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Madina, an 18-year-old Afghan girl, has faced immense challenges since the tragic murder of her mother at age 14 due to a family financial dispute. Left vulnerable, her father sought to marry her off to an older man in exchange for a bride for himself. Refusing the arrangement, Madina fled with her sisters to a safe house but was soon brought back home. Facing renewed threats of forced marriage and domestic violence, she escaped again, this time finding refuge at the Hagar Girls' Shelter.)
/E (Madina, an 18-year-old Afghan girl, has faced immense challenges since the tragic murder of her mother at age 14 due to a family financial dispute. Left vulnerable, her father sought to marry her off to an older man in exchange for a bride for himself. Refusing the arrangement, Madina fled with her sisters to a safe house but was soon brought back home. Facing renewed threats of forced marriage and domestic violence, she escaped again, this time finding refuge at the Hagar Girls' Shelter.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
528 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (At the shelter, Madina has found safe accommodation, regular psychosocial support, and a chance to continue her education, an opportunity denied to many girls in Afghanistan. She actively participates in drawing classes, educational programs, and vocational training in tailoring. Despite her father's attempts to bring her back, Madina remains determined to build her own future. She is committed to completing her education, securing a job, and choosing her life partner on her terms.)
/E (At the shelter, Madina has found safe accommodation, regular psychosocial support, and a chance to continue her education, an opportunity denied to many girls in Afghanistan. She actively participates in drawing classes, educational programs, and vocational training in tailoring. Despite her father's attempts to bring her back, Madina remains determined to build her own future. She is committed to completing her education, securing a job, and choosing her life partner on her terms.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
529 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Madina is deeply grateful to Hagar International for providing her a safe place and the support she needs to pursue a hopeful and independent future.)
