534 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Shashi is from West Bengal, where she lived with her parents in poverty. After completing up to Class 10, she had to discontinue her education to help her father on a farm. Her situation worsened when she was married to a man from her village who regularly abused her. After having a son, she eventually left her husband and returned to her parents' home, continuing to work on the farm.)
/E (Shashi is from West Bengal, where she lived with her parents in poverty. After completing up to Class 10, she had to discontinue her education to help her father on a farm. Her situation worsened when she was married to a man from her village who regularly abused her. After having a son, she eventually left her husband and returned to her parents' home, continuing to work on the farm.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
535 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (One day, Shashi met a woman who promised her a better job in Pune. Trusting the promise, she left her son with her parents and traveled to Pune with the woman, who turned out to be a trafficker. Shashi was introduced to a Spa owner who, under the pretense of employment, forced her into sexual exploitation. She was held for 12 days before being rescued by Rescue Foundation during an operation that also freed five other girls.)
/E (One day, Shashi met a woman who promised her a better job in Pune. Trusting the promise, she left her son with her parents and traveled to Pune with the woman, who turned out to be a trafficker. Shashi was introduced to a Spa owner who, under the pretense of employment, forced her into sexual exploitation. She was held for 12 days before being rescued by Rescue Foundation during an operation that also freed five other girls.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
